"""
freesoft-asr — live streaming speech recognition with an in-place
refining inline translation, in a terminal UI.

  # default (no args): transcribe whatever's playing on the default
  # sink's monitor; transcription only (no translation) unless a
  # config / flag asks for target languages:
  freesoft-asr

  # single-stream from stdin (any 16 kHz mono S16LE source):
  pw-record --target SOME_SOURCE --format=s16 --rate=16000 \
            --channels=1 - | freesoft-asr --source -
  freesoft-asr --source - --plain                    # headless log

  # named profile (a full config overlay). The built-in "dual" profile
  # is the author's two-stream RTP phone-call setup
  # (rtp_call_remote_source=Remote, rtp_call_me_source=Local):
  freesoft-asr --profile dual
  freesoft-asr --profile dual --plain
  freesoft-asr --list-profiles            # list available profiles

  # emit a fully-commented default config you can edit:
  freesoft-asr --write-config

Pipeline: audio -> Voxtral-Mini-4B-Realtime via a vLLM /v1/realtime WS
(raw transcription, language auto-detected by Voxtral); optionally
NLLB-200-distilled-600M int8 (CTranslate2, CPU) translates each
completed sentence into one or more configured target languages. The
source language of each sentence is auto-detected with fastText
(lid.176) unless pinned per-stream/globally with src_lang.

Sources are configurable (config file + CLI). Each source is a stream
with its own label, accent colour, optional src_lang override, and a
LIST of target languages (tgt_langs). A stream with no target languages
is transcription-only. The live region shows every active stream
stacked, always present and refining independently — no active-speaker
switching (a silent channel's sporadic deltas must not flip the panel).

Configuration is a TOML file at $XDG_CONFIG_HOME/freesoft-asr/
config.toml (default ~/.config/freesoft-asr/config.toml), overridable
with --config PATH. A [profiles.<name>] table is a FULL named overlay:
it may set any top-level key AND define its own [[profiles.<name>.source]]
streams. Select one with --profile NAME (or the default_profile config
key). Precedence: built-in defaults < config file < selected profile
overlay < CLI flags. A built-in "dual" profile reproduces the author's
phone-call setup with no config. `--write-config` emits a commented
default config that round-trips; `--list-profiles` lists profiles.

Audio is read from stdin (--source -), the default sink monitor, or
named PipeWire nodes via owned pw-record subprocesses, so the TUI
renders via ANSI to the terminal (stdout) and never reads stdin for
keys; quit with Ctrl-C (terminal is restored).
"""
